# Core Standards

## Naming

- Files and folders: **kebab-case** (`cancel-task-modal.tsx`, `checklist-builder/`)
- One main component per file; file name matches component (`CancelTaskModal` → `cancel-task-modal.tsx`)
- Props/API shapes: `I` prefix (`ITask`, `ICancelTaskModalData`)
- Generic/union types: `T` prefix when helpful (`TChipColor`, `TComponentSize`)

## TypeScript

- Function components with **`React.FC`** for main exports
- Strict mode; prefer explicit interfaces over `any`
- Use `type` imports for types only: `import type { ITask } from '...'`

## Imports

- **Relative paths from `src`** — no `@/` alias
- Order: React → external libs → internal (data, components, utils, types)

## Formatting (Prettier)

- 2 spaces, single quotes, `jsxSingleQuote: true`, print width 90
- Tailwind classes sorted via `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss`

## Scope

- Minimal diffs; match surrounding code before adding abstractions
- Reuse existing UI from `src/components/ui/` instead of raw HTML
- Comments only for non-obvious business logic
